==============================
LinkedIn Promotion
==============================

The algorithm doesn't know you already bought the thing. It just knows you keep clicking.

Recently, I realized I was spending hours watching reviews for tech I already owned instead of actually using it. I was trapped in "post-purchase rationalization"—chasing a borrowed dopamine hit instead of building the skill to use my tools.

The shift that helped me? Moving from passive consumption (watching reviews) to active learning (watching tutorials and mechanics deep-dives).

The best way to enjoy what you have is to use it — not to watch someone else talk about it.

Full thoughts on the blog today:

🔗 https://roobystudio.com/posts/post-purchase-rationalization/

==============================
X (Twitter) Promotion
==============================

Watching a 20-minute review video for a gadget that is literally sitting on the desk in front of you.

We all do it. It's called "post-purchase rationalization."

It’s like ordering food, the food arrives, and you just keep reading the menu.

Wrote about how to break the loop:

🔗 https://roobystudio.com/posts/post-purchase-rationalization/